{
  "question": "Acquire source-grounded evidence on transferring isolated-enzyme activity representations to control of steady-state metabolic pathway flux. Find research defining an isolated-enzyme rate law, research measuring how changing enzyme abundance or activity changes pathway flux, and a source-defined metabolic-control representation that could explain successes or failures of that transfer. Prefer a connected experimental system, such as microbial glycolysis, but do not assume that an intervention fails or that any enzyme is rate-limiting. Retain exact equations, assumptions, native quantities, experimental conditions, and source passages. Seek concrete comparisons of simple activity-based predictions with substrate adjustment, feedback, or distributed-control repairs, including successful predictions and information requirements. Whether these representations depend on a common generalized causal inference, and whether their differences establish pragmatic causal pluralism, remain questions for Scientific.",
